{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 41, :comments ["<b>And you shall clothe them, etc., and you shall anoint, etc.</b> Meaning: after he clothes them while the garments are still upon them, he shall anoint them, and not before; and through this the priesthood reaches their hand — which is what He means by <b>and you shall fill their hand</b>. Or perhaps in saying <b>their hand</b> He thereby intends to say that through the performance of the deed they are infused with the aspect of חסד, which pertains to the great hand — and understand:" "<b>And you shall sanctify.</b> Meaning: through the offering of the sacrifices, as He says: ״וְזֶה אֲשֶׁר תַּעֲשֶׂה לָהֶם לְקַדֵּשׁ אֹתָם״ (Exodus 29:1). And the reason He mentioned the matter here is to say that he should not sanctify them until he first performs the clothing and the anointing — and understand:"], :book :exodus, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 28, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:34:17.591342593Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}